  "body": "The archived selected PR1042 R480 program contains SCALE histories that can be consolidated across A/B stages while adjusting ADD coefficients and restoring the exact stage endpoint. This package selects 41 A and 22 B registers by explicit single-register cost scores, then emits and independently checks the composed full programs. Under retained PR696 lowering, scalar counts decrease 149002->148462 forward and 149018->148478 backward, saving 540 real scalar primitive operations per complex invocation in either orientation, combining both components (270 per component), with every boundary scale and private clearing charged. All paid frame events and their profile remain unchanged.\n\nBoth complete orientations pass all 704 arbitrary-column checks, exact independent stage maps, frame/wrapper replay, and primitive coefficient-work checks. Positive primitive-prefix bounds remain 52/68 bits. Ten controls include a useful failed alternative: blanket consolidation removes more macros but increases the strong forward count by 4264. The package claims a finite historical PR1042 construction, not optimal subset selection, native/hosted admission, a new precision theorem, or a changed kappa. PR750 and PR1064 are credited prior mechanisms; this is distinct from the concurrent fixed-helper gauge experiment.\n\nValidation: normal and optimized default saved-certificate replay; source-bound selected-result guard. Repository-wide `make verify` could not run because `make` is unavailable on this Windows host. See VALIDATION.md for exact commands and evidence.\n\nPrepared for @woklerx with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance. Apache-2.0.\n",
